    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "eaae43c5_8b0220f7",
        "filename": "cc/bp2build.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 159,
      "author": {
        "id": 1605027
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-06T21:31:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is unsuccessful in changing the targets generated in bionic/libc.\nI believe this is because header globbing is aggressive (`**/*.h`).\n\nA concrete example:\n\n\"libc_headers_arch\", has global include, \"kernel/uapi\", but arch include \"kernel/uapi/asm-arm\" for arm. \nSince the global include is a parent directory of the arch include, the global include captures all headers that the arch include intends to capture. As a result, the arch include has empty headers.",
      "revId": "50acbd5b40602eacad36b58efa74ca73cd638275",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dd3671bb_39d95fc2",
        "filename": "cc/bp2build.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 159,
      "author": {
        "id": 1726181
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-06T22:01:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This CL does two things\n\n- makes the includes be arch aware (to resolve http://b/183739834)\n- also makes the hdrs be arch aware\n\nAgree that the hdrs arch conditionals can sometimes be empty (if the base hdrs already contain all the headers that the arch would add). \n\nBut I wasn\u0027t sure if the globbing was actually too aggressive, or if the explictness of the converted BUILD files was actually revealing existing weirdness in the Android.bp files\n\nDo you think we should change the globs to be non-recursive?",
      "parentUuid": "eaae43c5_8b0220f7",
      "revId": "50acbd5b40602eacad36b58efa74ca73cd638275",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fd34bf5e_fec81471",
        "filename": "cc/bp2build.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 159,
      "author": {
        "id": 1605027
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-06T22:52:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure; I would also be fine with, for now, making all headers (even arch-specific headers), globally listed. This is the least strict approach, but, the closest matching Soong\u0027s non-sandbox behavior, for now. It seems thus lower priority to ensure that arch-specific header sources are handled correctly. (Arch-specific include paths, however, are still very important, and will be required to get successful builds of bionic)",
      "parentUuid": "dd3671bb_39d95fc2",
      "revId": "50acbd5b40602eacad36b58efa74ca73cd638275",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5efbde1e_882cfc6b",
        "filename": "cc/bp2build.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 159,
      "author": {
        "id": 1514900
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-07T03:39:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree with going with the recursive glob flattening approach for now, given that it doesn\u0027t deviate much from Soong and provides the same behavior for arch specific includes.",
      "parentUuid": "fd34bf5e_fec81471",
      "revId": "50acbd5b40602eacad36b58efa74ca73cd638275",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
